-- title:
--   Uniform bound for twisted orbital integrals of semi-local Hecke indicators
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every element of the Galois group lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (so $L/K$ is cyclic with generator $\sigma$), and let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal O_K$. The assertion is the existence of a constant $C \ge 0$ and an exponent $A \in \mathbb N$, depending only on these data, with the following property. Write $E_v = L \otimes_K K_v$, let $\mathcal K_v \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ be the set of $g$ such that both $g$ and $g^{-1}$ have all entries in the image of the semi-local integers of $L$ over $v$, and let $\mu'$ be the Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$, for the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of its topology, normalised by $\mu'(\mathcal K_v) = 1$. Then for every $a \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$; every $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ whose $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries vanish and whose diagonal entries satisfy $N_{E_v/K_v}(\delta_{00}) \neq N_{E_v/K_v}(\delta_{11})$; every Borel Haar measure $\tau'$ on the twisted centraliser $\{t \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v) : t\,\delta\,(\sigma t)^{-1} = \delta\}$ (where $\sigma$ acts entrywise through $\sigma \otimes 1$) giving mass $1$ to the elements of that subgroup lying in $\mathcal K_v$; and every $I \in \mathbb C$ that is a twisted orbital integral at $\delta$ against $\tau'$ of the indicator function of $\mathcal K_v \cdot \{a\} \cdot \mathcal K_v$ with value $1$, i.e. $I = \int \varphi(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x))\, w(x)\, \mathrm d\mu'(x)$ for some twisted section weight $w$ for these data, one has
--   $$\|N(\delta_{00}) - N(\delta_{11})\|\cdot\|I\| \le C\bigl(\|N(\delta_{00})N(\delta_{11})\| \cdot \mu'(\mathcal K_v a \mathcal K_v)\bigr)^{1/2}\bigl(1 + \log \mu'(\mathcal K_v a \mathcal K_v)\bigr)^{A},$$
--   the norms being those of $K_v$ and the volume being read as a real number.
--
--   This is the uniform-in-$a$ growth estimate for twisted orbital integrals of semi-local Hecke operators at regular diagonal (split-norm) classes in the cyclic base-change setting for $\mathrm{GL}_2$: the measure-theoretic prefactor $\|N\delta_{00}-N\delta_{11}\|$ is the twisted unipotent Jacobian, and the bound is by the square root of the double-coset volume times a power of its logarithm. It is used to derive the corresponding bound for indicators of double cosets and a coarser unweighted version of the same estimate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_forall_norm_sub_norm_mul_le_mul_rpow_mul_log_pow_of_isTwistedOrbitalIntegral_indicator_semiLocalIntegralSet_mul_mul.lean

